    "q-140476": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140476",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Rewrite $-8{z}^{2}-12z-\\frac{7}{2}$ by completing the square.",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the leading coefficient is $-8.$ So, we take out a factor of $-8$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n-8({z}^{2}+\\frac{3}{2}z+\\frac{7}{16})\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}+\\frac{3}{2}z+\\frac{7}{16}\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\cdot z+\\frac{7}{16}\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $\\frac{7}{16}$ last:\n\n$$\n{{z}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\cdot z+{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}+\\frac{7}{16}\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(z+\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}-{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}+\\frac{7}{16}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(z+\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{8}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8({z}^{2}+\\frac{3}{2}z+\\frac{7}{16}) & =-8({(z+\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =-8{(z+\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}+(-8)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =-8{(z+\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-140476-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-8{(z+\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}+1",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"37\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-msup><mjx-mrow><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-s3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28 TEX-S3\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D467 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mstyle space=\"3\"><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-num><mjx-dbox><mjx-dtable><mjx-line type=\"d\"></mjx-line><mjx-row><mjx-den><mjx-dstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-dstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-den></mjx-row></mjx-dtable></mjx-dbox></mjx-frac></mjx-mfrac></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-s3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29 TEX-S3\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-mrow><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 1.177em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn><msup><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\"><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
